## Quick Reference — Common `useradd` Flags

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `-u <UID>` | Set specific User ID |
| `-g <group>` | Set primary group |
| `-G <groups>` | Set supplementary groups |
| `-d <dir>` | Set home directory path |
| `-m` | Create home directory |
| `-M` | Do NOT create home directory |
| `-s <shell>` | Set login shell |
| `-c <comment>` | Add a comment/description |
| `-r` | Create a system account |

---

## Quick Reference — Common `usermod` Flags

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `-aG <group>` | Append user to a group (safe — doesn't remove existing groups) |
| `-s <shell>` | Change login shell |
| `-d <dir>` | Change home directory |
| `-u <UID>` | Change UID |
| `-l <name>` | Change username |
| `-L` | Lock the user account |
| `-U` | Unlock the user account |


